================================================================================
LESSON 9: ADDING LOADING STATE IN REACT
================================================================================


LESSON OVERVIEW
================================================================================

This lesson explains how to show loading feedback while books are being
fetched from an API.

Main concepts:

- Create an isLoading state
- Set loading to true before the API call
- Show a loading message or spinner
- Set loading to false after the request finishes
- Stop loading even when an error occurs
- Use finally to avoid duplicate code
- Use conditional rendering for different UI states


================================================================================
1. WHAT IS A LOADING STATE?
================================================================================

A loading state tells the application whether an asynchronous operation
is currently running.

Example:

const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false);


Values:

-------------------+------------------------------------------
isLoading         | Meaning
-------------------+------------------------------------------
false             | No API request is currently processing
true              | API request is currently processing
-------------------+------------------------------------------


When:

isLoading = true

Show:

Loading books...


When:

isLoading = false

Show:

Books / Error / No Results


