14. LOADING + ERROR + NO RESULTS + SUCCESS
================================================================================

A good application normally handles four UI states.


----------------+--------------------------------------+------------------------
State           | Condition                            | Display
----------------+--------------------------------------+------------------------
Loading         | isLoading                            | Loading indicator
Error           | !isLoading && error                  | Error message
No Results      | !isLoading && !error && books empty | No books message
Success         | !isLoading && !error && books exist | Book cards
----------------+--------------------------------------+------------------------


================================================================================
15. CONDITIONAL RENDERING
================================================================================

LOADING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{isLoading && (

  <div className="alert alert-info">
    Loading books...
  </div>

)}


ERROR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{!isLoading && error && (

  <div className="alert alert-danger">

    Error: {error}

  </div>

)}


NO RESULTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{!isLoading &&
 !error &&
 books.length === 0 && (

  <div className="alert alert-warning">

    No books found.

  </div>

)}


SUCCESS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

{!isLoading &&
 !error &&
 books.length > 0 && (

  <div className="row">

    {books.map((book) => (

      <div
        key={book.id}
        className="col-md-4 mb-4"
      >

        {book.volumeInfo?.title}

      </div>

    ))}

  </div>

)}


================================================================================
16. STATE TRANSITIONS
================================================================================

-------------------+-----------+---------------+-----------------+------------------
Stage              | isLoading | books         | error           | UI
-------------------+-----------+---------------+-----------------+------------------
Initial            | false     | []            | null            | No results*
Fetching           | true      | previous/[]   | null            | Loading
Success            | false     | [books...]    | null            | Book cards
Empty response     | false     | []            | null            | No books found
Failure            | false     | []            | Error message   | Error
-------------------+-----------+---------------+-----------------+------------------

*If you do not want "No books found" to appear before the first search,
you can maintain another state such as hasSearched.


================================================================================
17. OPTIONAL hasSearched STATE
================================================================================

Sometimes this initial UI is undesirable:

Page Opens
     |
     v
books.length === 0
     |
     v
"No books found"


But no search has happened yet.


Create:

const [hasSearched, setHasSearched] =
  useState(false);


After search completes:

setHasSearched(true);


No-results condition:

{hasSearched &&
 !isLoading &&
 !error &&
 books.length === 0 && (

  <div className="alert alert-warning">
    No books found.
  </div>

)}


This clearly separates:

"No search performed"

from:

"Search performed but returned zero books"


