20. DISABLE SEARCH BUTTON WHILE LOADING
================================================================================

While loading, it can be useful to prevent repeated searches.

Pass loading status to SearchBar:

<SearchBar
  searchTerm={searchTerm}
  onSearchChange={handleSearchChange}
  onSearch={handleSearchSubmit}
  isLoading={isLoading}
/>


Inside SearchBar:

function SearchBar({
  searchTerm,
  onSearchChange,
  onSearch,
  isLoading
}) {

  return (

    <form onSubmit={onSearch}>

      <div className="input-group">

        <input
          value={searchTerm}
          onChange={onSearchChange}
          className="form-control"
        />


        <button
          type="submit"
          className="btn btn-primary"
          disabled={isLoading}
        >

          {isLoading
            ? 'Searching...'
            : 'Search'}

        </button>

      </div>

    </form>

  );

}


Benefits:

- Prevents accidental duplicate searches.
- Provides additional visual feedback.
- Avoids multiple simultaneous requests from repeated clicks.


