23. DEBUGGING LOADING STATE
================================================================================

Common mistake:

setIsLoading(true);

console.log(isLoading);


You may expect:

true


But you may still see:

false


Reason:

- React schedules the state update.
- The current event handler belongs to the current render.
- Calling the setter does not mutate the existing variable immediately.


Better:

useEffect(() => {

  console.log(
    'Loading changed:',
    isLoading
  );

}, [isLoading]);


This observes committed changes to isLoading.


